    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Birch Creek Colony was founded in 1948 by Lehrerleut Hutterites seeking new farmland after Canadian overcrowding.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        4,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/birch_creek_colony_montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The colony thrives on livestock and dairy production, reflecting the Hutterite tradition of shared labor and self‑sufficient farming.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/birch_creek_colony_montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Farmers at Birch Creek Colony adjust crop schedules to guard against Montana’s harsh frosts and late‑summer heat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/birch_creek_colony_montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1963 and again in 1994, the colony split to create new Hutterite communities, keeping the original group sustainable.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
